7. SIXTH PHASE: LIVE GAMES AND SOCKET.IO

This is one of the most important integration areas.

Live games are delivered through Socket.IO, not through a documented live-games REST endpoint.

Connection:

wss://socket.smbet.net

Use the Socket.IO client library if it is not already installed.

Do not implement this as an ordinary WebSocket connection unless the server explicitly supports that protocol independently.

Documented events

The API documentation identifies the following event types:

1. buffers

Delivers full protobuf-encoded live game updates.

The updates contain game information, including odds, scores, time and match status.

2. buffer-diffs

Delivers incremental updates.

The currently documented integration has this handling disabled.

Do not assume incremental updates are already supported. Inspect the existing application and available decoding implementation before enabling them.

3. expired-key

Provides IDs of live matches that should be removed from the current live games collection.

